      "id": "k0khd2l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Force"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Force is an external push or pull that changes or tends to change the state of rest or uniform motion of a body.",
        "Work is defined as the scalar product of force and displacement (W = F × s × cos θ).",
        "Work can be positive, negative, or zero depending on the angle between the applied force and the direction of displacement.",
        "Power is the time rate of doing work (P = W / t), measured in Watts or Horsepower.",
        "Newton's First Law introduces inertia, the Second Law gives the formula F = ma, and the Third Law states action and reaction are equal and opposite."
      ],
      "id": "djytt5u"
    },
