    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "If a porter holds luggage on his head and walks horizontally on a platform, the work done against gravity is zero because the force and displacement are perpendicular (θ = 90°).",
        "Newton's First Law of Motion is frequently asked as the 'Law of Inertia'.",
        "Centripetal force acts towards the center in a circular path, whereas centrifugal force is a pseudo-force acting outwards.",
        "1 Horsepower (HP) is equal to 746 W, a standard conversion repeatedly tested in RRB, SSC, and state PSC exams."
      ],
